<urn:usf:acceptance:provider-capability-universe> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "usf status reports the derived universe with every candidate kind and the operator authorisation count, not the length of a configuration file. usf providers census and usf status agree on candidate identity and state for the same inputs. A work unit declaring a task-class capability routes to a route that has earned it and refuses when none has. A work unit declaring a model feature routes on catalogue evidence. A capability in neither vocabulary refuses under its own reason code. A route's task-class capabilities come only from qualification records bound to that route. The economic admission that governs execution also governs the availability preflight, and no path admits a cost class the policy refuses." <urn:usf:graph:provider-capability-universe> .
